# Plan — documentary reconciliation and operational F0 gate

D-01 [REQ-01,04]: archive exact inputs and map evidence dependencies before editing; task completion records an existing bounded consumer result, not new product acceptance. R-01: false freshness by rehashing old results or borrowing aggregated approval.
D-02 [REQ-02]: preserve the seven F0 rows, separate adopted policies from proposed milestone criteria and require maintainer adoption before closure. R-02: reducing a gate to fit existing code or turning a roadmap into authorization.
D-03 [REQ-03]: compare storage alternatives against the same integrity/failure corpus and create a proposed feature only. R-03: assuming SQLite adoption or implementing before permission.
D-04 [REQ-04]: new documentary inspections bind current contracts; historical execution inputs that changed are retained under exact-byte snapshot paths with their old digests. R-04: silently changing the identity/scope of historical execution. Original complete envelopes survive under before/; archive paths are explicitly mapped. No code/oracle change means no automatic full replay.

Primary selected/consulted/used: autonomous-verification-engineering, .codex/skills/autonomous-verification-engineering/SKILL.md (no declared version), sdd/chain/autonomous-verification-engineering.md bridge_version 1. Question: criterion authority, independent oracles, input dependencies and false operational acceptance. Contribution: F0 matrix, separate states, selective evidence comparison and negative gate checks. Supporting distinct question: database-engineering, .codex/skills/database-engineering/SKILL.md (no declared version), sdd/chain/database-engineering.md bridge_version 1, references/model-and-transactions.md; contribution: common storage invariants, alternative costs and recovery contract. No delegated agent work or recursive skill activation.

Alternatives rejected: checkbox-only reconciliation ignores bound inputs; whole-suite rerun does not establish semantic succession; adopting storage to close F0 invents authority; replacing history hides failures. Retain the 25-row starting matrix and annotate only affected legacy obligations. Named successor ADRs do not automatically expand their stated adoption scope.

Observed source/skill versions are content hashes in docs/validation/f0-reconciliation-20261101/inputs-final.json. Commands verified from README, project and actual scripts: validate.py structure/fresh modes, check-ox.py, verify-maintenance.py, unittest test_technical_acceptance and test_reconciliation. Reuse existing Cargo/GUI observations only as inherited records; code and oracles are unchanged. Structural success does not accept operational F0. Current package qualification is not performed unless needed by an adopted distribution gate.

## Recovery integration discovered by focused checks

D-05 [REQ-04]: the existing recovery checker cannot resolve changed task/spec inputs through its translation-only mapping. Add a bounded documentary predecessor map (17 paths), retaining original hashes and unknown-mutation rejection. No product source/storage change. New module tests cover positive recovery, unknown current bytes, corrupt/missing/escaping predecessor, extra/missing/duplicate scope and unrelated input. Run existing recovery tests against the updated helper and preserve failures. The pre-edit foundation/layout plan/task review appendices also required authenticated historical recovery; this does not retroactively validate the inherited baseline.

The recovered Portuguese tasks are derived by removing only the preexisting T900 appendix and matching the existing maintenance digest; translated plans use their already authenticated translation predecessors. Full pre-edit bytes remain in before/. Selection remains criterion/evidence engineering; no additional skill is activated.
